<speak>We can absolutely leave room for pauses. You can simply say you're making a note, and I'll wait. If I genuinely can't hear you, I'll say so, rather than interpreting a quiet moment as anything else. For administrative explanations, I can give one point at a time. That is different from repeating all the substantive content, and it keeps your notes less crowded. We don't need to turn every pause into another question. A telephone conversation can be comfortable without filling every second.</speak>